  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 42a7ef911f4c60e408989a759d2b9b18, type: 3}
  m_Name: PY_BOOLEAN
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::CodeEscape.Programming.LessonData
  id: PY_BOOLEAN
  language: 1
  conceptTitle: 'Boolean Logic: and, or, not'
  symbol: and
  relatedQuestionIds:
  - PY_06_BOOLEAN
  - HZ_PY_03_BOOLEAN
  - PY_RUN_10_BOOLEAN
  topics:
  - Boolean Logic
  definition: Boolean logic works with the values True and False. It lets a program
    combine several conditions into one answer.
  howItWorks: 'and is True only when both sides are True. or is True when at least
    one side is True. not flips a value: not True is False and not False is True.
    Work out not first, then and, then or.'
  exampleCode: 'raining = False

    umbrella = True

    stay_dry = not raining
    or umbrella

    go_out = raining and not umbrella

    print(stay_dry, go_out)'
  exampleExplanation: 'not raining flips False to True, so stay_dry is True or True,
    which is True. go_out needs raining to be True, but it is False, so the whole
    and is False. The program prints: True False'
  tip: For and, check both sides. For or, one True side is enough.
